<title>GERMANY: GERMAN JAN-APRIL COCOA IMPORTS UP AT 100,430 T.</title>
<headline>GERMAN JAN-APRIL COCOA IMPORTS UP AT 100,430 T.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cocoa bean imports from third countries in January/April 1997 totalled 100,430 tonnes after 94,544 tonnes in the same 1996 period, federal statistics office data showed.</p>
<p>Imports in April were 15,706 tonnes compared with 47,048 tonnes in March and 24,951 tonnes in April 1996.</p>
<p>The data did not include volumes received via other European Union countries.</p>
<p>Leading supplier Ivory Coast shipped a total 65,379 tonnes in the four months, followed by Ghana's 14,855, Indonesia's 9,016 and Nigeria's 5,195.</p>
<p>January-April import value (third countries only) of 229.5 million marks compared with 207.9 million the year before.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
